# Session 1: Phase 0 (Skeleton Implementation)

## Purpose
Execute Session 1 to create a fully functional Spring Boot skeleton where all endpoints return mock DTOs matching the OpenAPI specification. This establishes project structure, enables `@WebMvcTest` writing, and validates API contracts.

## CRITICAL: This Session Stops After Skeleton - No Endpoint Implementation

DO NOT:
- Implement real business logic
- Create Flyway migrations
- Create `@Entity` classes
- Create `JpaRepository` interfaces or `@Service` classes with real logic
- Proceed to Session 2 automatically

ONLY:
- Create Maven project structure
- Implement mock `@RestController` endpoints
- Set up Docker Compose
- Configure `application.yml`
- Create `@WebMvcTest` scaffolding

Session 2 (first real endpoint implementation) is a SEPARATE session that requires explicit user command.

## Session Prerequisites
- OpenAPI specification complete and validated
- Plan folder structure created with session plans
- Session 1 plan reviewed (`plan/sessions/session-1-phase-0.md`)
- Maven wrapper working, JDK pinned (see `rules/000-environment-setup.mdc`)

