### 5. Mock Endpoint Implementation

For each endpoint in the OpenAPI spec, create a mock `@RestController` method.

**Pattern for POST endpoints:**
```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/posts")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class PostController {

    @PostMapping
    public ResponseEntity<PostResponse> createPost(@Valid @RequestBody CreatePostRequest request) {
        // MOCK IMPLEMENTATION — Phase 0 skeleton
        PostResponse mock = new PostResponse(
            UUID.fromString("00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000123"),
            request.title(),
            request.content(),
            request.authorId(),
            Instant.parse("2024-01-01T00:00:00Z")
        );
        return ResponseEntity.ok(mock);
    }
}
```

**Pattern for GET endpoints:**
```java
@GetMapping("/{postId}")
public ResponseEntity<PostResponse> getPost(@PathVariable UUID postId) {
    // MOCK IMPLEMENTATION — Phase 0 skeleton
    PostResponse mock = new PostResponse(
        postId,
        "Mock Post Title",
        "Mock post content here",
        UUID.fromString("00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000aa"),
        Instant.parse("2024-01-01T00:00:00Z")
    );
    return ResponseEntity.ok(mock);
}
```

### 6. Request/Response DTOs
Create Java `record` DTOs matching OpenAPI schemas.

```java
public record CreatePostRequest(
    @NotBlank @Size(max = 200) String title,
    @NotBlank String content,
    @NotNull UUID authorId
) {}

public record PostResponse(
    UUID postId,
    String title,
    String content,
    UUID authorId,
    Instant createdAt
) {}
```

Field names are camelCase to match the JSON contract by default — no aliasing layer is needed since Jackson serializes Java record component names directly.

### 7. OpenAPI / Swagger UI
Add `springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui` to `pom.xml` so mock endpoints are immediately browsable:
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
    <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
    <version>2.6.0</version>
</dependency>
```
This exposes interactive docs at `/swagger-ui.html` with zero extra configuration — the Phase 0 equivalent of FastAPI's automatic `/docs`.

### 8. Testing Setup
Create test structure:
```
src/test/java/com/example/<app>/
├── web/
│   ├── HealthControllerTest.java
│   └── PostControllerTest.java
└── ApplicationTests.java
```

Add a minimal `@WebMvcTest` stub:
```java
@WebMvcTest(PostController.class)
class PostControllerTest {

    @Autowired
    private MockMvc mockMvc;

    @Test
    void createPost_returnsOk() throws Exception {
        mockMvc.perform(post("/api/posts")
                .contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
                .content("""
                    {"title":"Test","content":"Body","authorId":"00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000aa"}
                    """))
            .andExpect(status().isOk());
    }
}
```

