## Mock Data Guidelines

### Consistency
Use consistent mock IDs across related endpoints:
- Post ID: `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000123`
- Author ID: `00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000aa`
- Comment ID: `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000456`

### Realistic Structure
Mock responses should match production structure:
- Include all required fields
- Use proper Java types (`UUID`, `Instant`, not raw `String`)
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes

### Error Cases
Implement mock error responses via the global exception handler:
```java
@GetMapping("/{postId}")
public ResponseEntity<PostResponse> getPost(@PathVariable UUID postId) {
    if (postId.toString().equals("00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000")) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND, "Post not found");
    }
    return ResponseEntity.ok(mockResponse);
}
```

